<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">9 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 9 March, from 1074 to 1945.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1074 CE <span class="tih-ago">952 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gregory VII's synod condemns married and simoniac priests</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At his Lenten synod in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-vii">Pope Gregory VII</a> barred married priests and those who had bought office from ministering. The reforms helped impose clerical celibacy in the Western Church.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-alvares-cabral" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-alvares-cabral.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1500">1500 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">526 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pedro Álvares Cabral sails from Lisbon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cabral's fleet of 13 ships left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, swinging far west into the Atlantic. On 22 April it sighted the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>, which Cabral claimed for Portugal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-alvares-cabral">Pedro Álvares Cabral</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1796">1796 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">230 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon Bonaparte marries Joséphine de Beauharnais</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The civil wedding in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> took place two days before <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> left to command the Army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>. Joséphine became empress in 1804, but he divorced her in 1810 for lack of an heir.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1841">1841 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">185 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Supreme Court frees the Amistad Africans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Court ruled that the Mende captives who had seized the slave ship Amistad had been illegally enslaved. Argued by John Quincy Adams, the case became a cause for abolitionists.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1862">1862 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">164 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Monitor and Virginia fight the first battle between ironclads</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Hampton Roads, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>, USS Monitor and the Confederate CSS Virginia fought for hours without decisive damage. The duel showed that wooden warships were obsolete.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pancho Villa raids Columbus, New Mexico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Some 500 of Villa's fighters attacked the border town, killing 18 Americans. The US sent General John Pershing on a punitive expedition into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, which failed to catch Villa.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US firebombing raid devastates Tokyo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the night of 9-10 March, some 300 B-29 bombers dropped incendiaries on Tokyo, burning about 41 square kilometres. Around 100,000 people died, the deadliest air raid in history.</p></div></li></ol>
